{"on": "session/prompt", "send": [{"notify": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_df3c3e455ffe3KZVShQ00LZ15D", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_thought_chunk", "messageId": "msg_20c3c2cd100128V07kJYjWiXYd:reasoning:0", "content": {"type": "text", "text": "I will write a 500-word essay on the history of the ls command using only my own knowledge, with no external tools."}}}}, {"notify": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_df3c3e455ffe3KZVShQ00LZ15D", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "messageId": "msg_20c3c2cd100128V07kJYjWiXYd", "content": {"type": "text", "text": "# The History of the `ls` Command\n\nThe `ls` command is one of the oldest and most familiar tools in the Unix tradition. Its name is simply an abbreviation of “list,” and its job"}}}}, {"notify": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_df3c3e455ffe3KZVShQ00LZ15D", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "messageId": "msg_20c3c2cd100128V07kJYjWiXYd", "content": {"type": "text", "text": " has always been the same: show the names of files in a directory. That"}}}}, {"notify": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_df3c3e455ffe3KZVShQ00LZ15D", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "messageId": "msg_20c3c2cd100128V07kJYjWiXYd", "content": {"type": "text", "text": " modest purpose is why it survived more than half a century of"}}}}, {"notify": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_df3c3e455ffe3KZVShQ00LZ15D", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "messageId": "msg_20c3c2cd100128V07kJYjWiXYd", "content": {"type": "text", "text": " operating-system change, from the lab machines"}}}}, {"notify": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_df3c3e455ffe3KZVShQ00LZ15D", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "messageId": "msg_20c3c2cd100128V07kJYjWiXYd", "content": {"type": "text", "text": " of the late 1960s to the containers"}}}}, {"notify": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_df3c3e455ffe3KZVShQ00LZ15D", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "messageId": "msg_20c3c2cd100128V07kJYjWiXYd", "content": {"type": "text", "text": " and cloud hosts of today.\n\n`ls` belongs to the first generation of Unix"}}}}, {"notify": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_df3c3e455ffe3KZVShQ00LZ15D", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "messageId": "msg_20c3c2cd100128V07kJYjWiXYd", "content": {"type": "text", "text": " userland programs written at Bell Labs."}}}}, {"notify": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_df3c3e455ffe3KZVShQ00LZ15D", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "messageId": "msg_20c3c2cd100128V07kJYjWiXYd", "content": {"type": "text", "text": " Ken Thompson and Dennis Ritchie, working on"}}}}, {"notify": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_df3c3e455ffe3KZVShQ00LZ15D", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "messageId": "msg_20c3c2cd100128V07kJYjWiXYd", "content": {"type": "text", "text": " a PDP-7 and then a PDP-11, needed a way to inspect"}}}}, {"notify": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_df3c3e455ffe3KZVShQ00LZ15D", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "messageId": "msg_20c3c2cd100128V07kJYjWiXYd", "content": {"type": "text", "text": " the directories their new filesystem produced. Early"}}}}, {"notify": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_df3c3e455ffe3KZVShQ00LZ15D", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "messageId": "msg_20c3c2cd100128V07kJYjWiXYd", "content": {"type": "text", "text": " Unix treated a directory as a special file whose contents were names paired with"}}}}, {"waitFor": "session/cancel"}, {"notify": "session/update", "params": {"sessionId": "ses_df3c3e455ffe3KZVShQ00LZ15D", "update": {"sessionUpdate": "agent_message_chunk", "messageId": "msg_20c3c2cd100128V07kJYjWiXYd", "content": {"type": "text", "text": " inode numbers. Listing those names was not a shell"}}}}], "reply": {"stopReason": "cancelled", "_meta": {}}}
